# The demo path

Twenty minutes. Always lead with the AI.

---

# Demo screen #1 — Mapping Studio

![bg right:58%](screens/cashhub-mapping-studio.png)

Open Mapping Studio. Drop in a carrier statement PDF. Wait three seconds.

- Show the AI's proposed column mappings
- Show the "valid license" link in the corner (HSO licenses on productization)
- Click Accept; the template saves
- Run extraction → preview rows
- *"This used to be a two-day analyst task."*

---

# Demo screen #2 — Cash Application Review

![bg right:58%](screens/cashhub-cash-applications.png)

Open a Cash Application header. Walk the room through the matched lines.

- Approved lines tinted green
- Match Status badge: Auto / Manual / Requires Review
- Multi-select toolbar: Approve all visible, Unapprove, Unmatch
- *"The matching engine learns from every manual fix."*

---

# Demo screen #3 — Compensation Actuals

![bg right:58%](screens/comphub-comp-actuals.png)

Switch to CompHub. Show the comp batch list with workflow status pills.

- Filter by Submitted / In Progress / Approved
- Drill into a batch — payable lines per producer
- Show invoice IDs auto-generated on the Approved transition
- *"Producer comp out of the spreadsheet, into the audit trail."*

---

# Demo flow — the 20-minute version

The order matters. Lead with the magic; finish with the math.

- **5 min — Mapping Studio.** Drop in a carrier statement PDF. AI suggests the columns. Click accept. Done.
- **5 min — Cash Application Review.** Open a header. Show matched lines. Approve. Show parent/child splits.
- **3 min — Research Cases.** The unmatched cash. Assignable, notes-able, audit-trailed.
- **4 min — Compensation Actuals.** Show batch detail, invoice IDs auto-generated on approval.
- **3 min — Producer Portal.** Switch hat — log in as a producer. See your own statement.

*Net: by minute 12 they're asking about pricing.*

